WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.163 --> 00:00:01.427
(audience cheers)

00:00:01.427 --> 00:00:03.849
- [Conan] My guests tonight
are the stars and creators

00:00:03.849 --> 00:00:06.400
of the Emmy Award winning
HBO series "Game of Thrones".

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.658
Please welcome Executive
Producers, D.B. Weiss,

00:00:08.658 --> 00:00:12.478
David Benioff, and from
the cast, Iwan Rheon,

00:00:12.478 --> 00:00:15.538
Conleth Hill, Nathalie
Emmanuel, (inaudible),

00:00:15.538 --> 00:00:18.337
Liam Cunningham, John
Bradley, Kristian Nairn,

00:00:18.337 --> 00:00:19.874
Isaac Hempstead Wright.

00:00:19.874 --> 00:00:21.264
There you go, I had to get them all out.

00:00:21.264 --> 00:00:22.792
Thank you.

00:00:22.792 --> 00:00:25.123
So cool, how ya doin'?

00:00:25.123 --> 00:00:26.040
How are ya?

00:00:28.432 --> 00:00:30.515
Thank you for being here.

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:45.940
Hey, good to see ya, how are you?

00:00:51.116 --> 00:00:53.366
(applause)

00:01:03.734 --> 00:01:05.784
Well, that's nice. (laughs)

00:01:05.784 --> 00:01:08.034
(applause)

00:01:15.438 --> 00:01:16.657
Well, that's all the time we have.

00:01:16.657 --> 00:01:18.804
Thank you so much.

00:01:18.804 --> 00:01:20.798
You know there's one
mistake I made last year,

00:01:20.798 --> 00:01:22.876
I am not gonna make it again.

00:01:22.876 --> 00:01:25.543
Last year, Liam, I ran
out of time before I got

00:01:25.543 --> 00:01:28.009
to ask you a question.

00:01:28.009 --> 00:01:31.005
It bothered me very much,
so I'm going to start

00:01:31.005 --> 00:01:32.200
with you this year.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:33.196
Okay, how about that?

00:01:33.196 --> 00:01:34.578
How do you feel about that, Liam?

00:01:34.578 --> 00:01:36.828
(applause)

00:01:39.426 --> 00:01:40.819
- Good move, dude.

00:01:40.819 --> 00:01:41.652
- Good move?

00:01:41.652 --> 00:01:43.986
- Oh yeah, I got a
blunt machete backstage.

00:01:43.986 --> 00:01:46.213
You were gonna lose a limb
if you didn't talk to me.

00:01:46.213 --> 00:01:47.446
(laughs)

00:01:47.446 --> 00:01:49.598
- Stop glowering at me, for God's sake.

00:01:49.598 --> 00:01:51.025
All right, I gotta ask you, Liam,

00:01:51.025 --> 00:01:52.983
you have lasted five seasons.

00:01:52.983 --> 00:01:55.290
What is the secret to not getting killed

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:57.445
on "Game of Thrones"?

00:01:57.445 --> 00:01:58.278
What is it?

00:01:58.278 --> 00:02:01.278
(applause)

00:02:01.278 --> 00:02:02.630
- All right, let me
tell you, those two boys

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:05.391
down the end there have
got a sick sense of humor.

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:06.929
- Yeah.

00:02:06.929 --> 00:02:08.987
- They're like the, you can compare them

00:02:08.987 --> 00:02:11.684
to the heads of the five
families in New York.

00:02:11.684 --> 00:02:12.761
- Right, right.

00:02:12.761 --> 00:02:14.988
- You get a phone call to go to dinner.

00:02:14.988 --> 00:02:15.821
- Right.

00:02:15.821 --> 00:02:16.801
- You don't come back from that dinner.

00:02:16.801 --> 00:02:18.982
(laughs)

00:02:18.982 --> 00:02:21.534
So, the trick is, don't make eye contact,

00:02:21.534 --> 00:02:22.521
don't pick up the phone.

00:02:22.521 --> 00:02:24.382
- Don't pick up the phone,
don't make eye contact,

00:02:24.382 --> 00:02:26.965
don't talk to them, very, very wise.

00:02:26.965 --> 00:02:29.067
How would you like to see Davos go,

00:02:29.067 --> 00:02:31.294
when he goes, how would
you like to see him go?

00:02:31.294 --> 00:02:32.408
- Well, I've made a couple of suggestions.

00:02:32.408 --> 00:02:34.080
I think he should go to Dorne,

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:37.495
he should drink some vintage Dornish wine

00:02:37.495 --> 00:02:41.150
in the company of a couple
of hookers and an eight ball.

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:45.317
(laughs)
(applause)

00:02:47.283 --> 00:02:49.409
I'm not sure what an
eight ball is but there.

